 "diagnosis": "The loop invariant '0 <= i <= (l) + 1' is too loose. Since the loop guard is 'i < l' and the body does 'i := i + 1', i can never exceed l after an iteration. With the loose bound, after the loop we only know 'l <= i <= l+1' instead of 'i == l'. This means: (1) the slice 'ns[..i]' in the invariant is not well-formed since i could be ns.Length+1, and (2) the bridge fails because 'is_sorted(ns[..i])' with i possibly equal to l+1 does not imply the postcondition 'is_sorted(ns[..])' where ns[..] == ns[..ns.Length] == ns[..l]. The fix is to change the invariant to '0 <= i <= l'."}

